# 1v1, cloud locks to the PC (BENCH-253), round 15: two cloud locks from 21 Nov morning, RamRod on rbd (RAM-18 escape
# bend) and Saguaro on rp (POW-17 race power), plus 12 more seeds for round 14's three marginal rammers on rbd.
# Round 14 (PR #964) held rbd on 6 of its 11 rammers and rf on ScalpBotC; GrubbmThree +1.6, MaxRisk +1.0 and
# PureAggression +0.8 read positive with the 95% low end under 0 (the marginal rule: 12 more seeds); Sabreur -0.8 is
# dropped. Leopard read -0.6 on the PC but locked on 12 fresh cloud seeds afterwards (84300, below), so it gets a
# second PC read.
# Cloud locks (master, Robocode 1.12.0, live turn time; coverage/shards/locks.tsv):
#   rbd on RamRod (box A, coverage/shards/dzlane/A/power4): 12 fresh seeds 81300 +3.10 +- 2.13 against c and +2.33 +- 1.90
#      against aa; screen 81200 +5.0 / +1.6.
#   rbd on GrubbmThree, MaxRisk and PureAggression (round 14 PC, 12 seeds 85000): +1.59, +0.96, +0.76. The gate reads
#      round 15 alone; the bank pools rounds 14 and 15 (24 PC seeds) for these three and keeps a line only where the
#      pooled 95% low end is above 0. On the cloud screen's truth logs (rbend, 6 seeds) the bend cut their close-range
#      (<150 px) hit rate on GrubbmThree 53 -> 45% and PureAggression 66 -> 53%; MaxRisk stayed at 41% but its
#      linear-aimed close shots fell from 46% to 34% hits.
#   rbd on Leopard (box L, coverage/shards/dzlane/L/rbend-r14): 12 fresh cloud seeds 84300 +1.54 +- 0.59 against c (24
#      control battles) and +1.16 +- 0.75 against aa; the class screen read +0.78. It was picked from a re-read of round 14's 5 misses (Sabreur and MaxRisk did
#      not lock), so round 15 is its only independent check. The gate reads round 15 alone;
#      the bank pools rounds 14 and 15 and keeps the line only where the pooled 95% low end is above 0.
#   rp (POW-17 race power) on Saguaro (boxes A and L): pooled 60 seeds (81300-81347, 84000-84011) +4.76 +- 2.64 against c
#      and +3.26 +- 2.29 against aa (A/A +1.50 +- 2.69); screen 81200 +11.2 / +6.3.
#   livematch  the released jar and BeepBoop 2.0 on the 31-robot panel at the live constant, read against live
#   lock       panel-locks.txt  c / aa / rbd / rp, 12 fresh seeds from 85100, --cpu-constant live, in work/pc-locks15
#              (earlier rounds' battles stay in work/pc-locks to -locks14)
#   gate       each robot judged on its own arm only (lock_prep.py --restrict); it keeps its line where the 95% low end
#              is above 0 (mode_table.py --margin 0).
# Leigh starts it once the PC is free (one card at a time, from master):
#   git checkout master && git pull
#   .\queue.ps1 run pc-locks --fresh        (or  ./queue.sh run pc-locks --fresh)
#   --fresh because round 14 left this plan's queue state marked complete; an interrupted round 15 resumes without it.
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, 16 workers, truth log off. 288 lock battles (6 robots, 4 arms, 12 seeds), about
# 15 minutes with the live-match check.
#
# Why it should win (the PC card rule of 2026-11-03):
#   - Per-opponent tailoring: every line names one robot; every other robot, team and melee play bit for bit as master
#     (RAM-18 only acts inside RAM-2's rammer escape and POW-17 only sets fire power, in a duel, against a robot the table
#     names).
#   - RAM-18 is on master since round 14 (PR #964 held it on 6 rammers): for 10 ticks after each rammer shot the escape
#     leaves out headings within 25 degrees of the line we were on when it fired, because RAM-2's fixed-heading escape
#     is the path a linear aim leads (linear aim would hit us 32% under 150 px vs BeepBoop 10%).
#   - RamRod: its hits on us land almost all while RAM-2's escape runs and are unplanned (box A truth logs, 6 seeds
#     81400), the same fixed-heading escape RAM-18 bends; rbd beat rf on it on both the screen and the lock.
#   - Saguaro: an energy race. BeepBoop holds power 0.7-0.85 whatever the energies, its rounds run longer, and it wins
#     them; we open at 2.0 and lose the race (box A truth logs, 6 seeds 81400). POW-17's race power is the table's
#     existing answer to an energy race; on the cloud it beat the POW-20 power band on Saguaro against both twins.
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md): the watcher's A/A rule needs 10 robots read in both c and aa, which this six-robot lock
# never reaches, so no aa stop rule is set; aa is read in the gate (multiarm.py prints aa against c). The lock halts on 30 failed
# battles, an arm scoring nothing in 8, 60+ skipped turns a battle over the last 24 or no battle in 30 minutes. The
# live-match step stops the card if the PC no longer scores us and BeepBoop as live does (tools/live_match.py exit 3).
# ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on any stop.
# Bank: the owning cloud thread adds the gate's lines on this card's results PR. Nothing is released by the card.
set V = 3.23
set P = --parallel 16 --no-truth-log --failed-ok
set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant live --child-heap 2G
set W = work/pc-locks15
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p bisect work && (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests package) && cp ../hadur-robot/target/hadur117.Hadur_${V}.jar bisect/ && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && python3 tools/lock_prep.py plans/locks-pick.tsv panel-locks.txt plans/pc-locks.arms ${W}-prep && bash ${W}-prep/build.sh && for a in rbd rp; do test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}$a.jar || exit 1; done && bash tools/fetch_live_jar.sh && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-r31.txt && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set livematch-bb.txt && test -f opponents/kc.mega.BeepBoop_2.0.jar && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-locks.txt && mvn -q compile

livematch | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-r31.txt --seeds 2 --seed-base 21700 --arms plans/livematch.arms --out work/pc-livematch-rel-live --label pc-locks-livematch --shuffle-jobs && python3 tools/live_match.py work/pc-livematch-rel-live/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/pc-locks15-livematch.md
  after: prep
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-locks.txt --seeds 12 --seed-base 85100 --arms ${W}-prep/lock.arms --out ${W} --label pc-locks --shuffle-jobs
  after: livematch
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 60 over 24
  stop: stall 30m

gate | python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks15-lock.md && python3 tools/lock_prep.py --restrict ${W}/arms.tsv ${W}-prep ${W}/arms-picked.tsv && python3 ../data/tools/mode_table.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --margin 0 --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks15-lock-pick.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks15-lock-pick.md && python3 tools/per_robot.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --arms rbd rp --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks15-lock-per-robot.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks15-lock-per-robot.tsv
  after: lock

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-locks15-results "1v1 cloud locks, round 15 (5 robots on rbd, 1 on rp) locked on 12 fresh PC seeds" ${OUT}/pc-locks15-livematch.md ${OUT}/*_pc-locks15-*.md ${OUT}/pc-locks15-lock-per-robot.tsv $(find ${OUT} -maxdepth 1 -name 'pc-locks15-lock-pick.tsv' -size +0c)
  after: gate
